   "SpecificHeat": 712,
   "Source": "Relative permittivity 11.9: Sze and Ng, Physics of Semiconductor Devices, properties of Si at 300 K. Loss tangent at 10 GHz derived for 10 kohm-cm resistivity from tan d = sigma / (omega eps0 epsr); lower-resistivity silicon is lossier in proportion. Thermal conductivity 148 W/(m K) at 300 K, density 2329 kg/m3 and specific heat 712 J/(kg K) at 25 C: CRC Handbook of Chemistry and Physics. Silicon's conductivity falls with temperature (roughly as T^-1.3); no table is stated here.",
